# Source: https://github.com/nf-core/sarek/issues/1148
#   https://github.com/nf-core/sarek/issues/1389
# Symptom: GATK/Picard interval-scatter pipelines interpret the 5th column
#   (designated "score" in BED) as a timing/weight hint for scatter interval
#   sizing.  When this column contains elapsed-seconds values (e.g. 12.5,
#   3600.0) from a profiled run, the scatter algorithm creates an absurd number
#   of sub-intervals (hundreds of thousands instead of dozens), paralysing the
#   pipeline.  Score must be an integer 0-1000; floating-point timing values
#   are semantically invalid and operationally catastrophic in this context.
chr1	10000	50000	target001	12.5	.
chr1	50001	200000	target002	3600.0	.
chr2	1000	80000	target003	0.3	.
chr3	500000	1000000	target004	7200.1	.
